      "formula": "joint_execution_fidelity / solo_execution_fidelity",
      "forbid_proxy_substitution": true,
      "fail_on_semantic_downgrade": true,
      "notes": "The reproduction may reduce sample count or shots for runtime, but it must preserve Fig. 11(c)'s per-application comparison by aggregating component relative fidelities from the selected QOS pair-set joint simulations. It must fail instead of falling back to representative single-pair or single-circuit application proxies."
    }
  },
  "expected_trend": "QOS M/P should produce all three Fig. 11 outputs, cover all three methods and utilization thresholds, include nine benchmark applications, render Fig. 11(c) as per-application relative-fidelity bars by utilization, improve fidelity over the baselines, improve effective utilization over baseline M/P, preserve selected-pair-set multiprogramming semantics of relative fidelity, and keep relative fidelity loss bounded.",
